compilePlan.emissionStrategy:
## NEW ADT EMISSION — Sealed-interface + Variant Structs

The runtime gains a marker method `_sky_adt_<TypeName>()` so Go's structural subtyping makes a sealed interface per ADT. Every variant is its own concrete struct with typed fields (no `Fields []any`). A constructor function literally returns the variant struct; Go auto-widens to the interface at use sites — no rt.Coerce.

### (a) Monomorphic ADT: `type Color = Red | Green | RGB Int Int Int`

```go
// ── Sealed interface (the "ADT type") ────────────────────────────
type Main_Color interface {
    _sky_adt_Main_Color()
    SkyName() string                       // for msgDisplayName + gob
}

// ── Per-variant concrete structs ─────────────────────────────────
type Main_Color_Red_V   struct{}
type Main_Color_Green_V struct{}
type Main_Color_RGB_V   struct{ V0, V1, V2 int }

func (Main_Color_Red_V)   _sky_adt_Main_Color() {}
func (Main_Color_Green_V) _sky_adt_Main_Color() {}
func (Main_Color_RGB_V)   _sky_adt_Main_Color() {}

func (Main_Color_Red_V)   SkyName() string { return "Red" }
func (Main_Color_Green_V) SkyName() string { return "Green" }
func (Main_Color_RGB_V)   SkyName() string { return "RGB" }

// ── Constructors return concrete; widen automatically ────────────
var Main_Color_Red   Main_Color = Main_Color_Red_V{}
var Main_Color_Green Main_Color = Main_Color_Green_V{}
func Main_Color_RGB(v0, v1, v2 int) Main_Color {
    return Main_Color_RGB_V{V0: v0, V1: v1, V2: v2}
}

// ── Gob + runtime tag registry (init) ────────────────────────────
func init() {
    rt.RegisterAdtVariant("Main_Color", "Red",   0, Main_Color_Red_V{})
    rt.RegisterAdtVariant("Main_Color", "Green", 1, Main_Color_Green_V{})
    rt.RegisterAdtVariant("Main_Color", "RGB",   2, Main_Color_RGB_V{})
    gob.Register(Main_Color_Red_V{})
    gob.Register(Main_Color_Green_V{})
    gob.Register(Main_Color_RGB_V{})
}
```

### (b) Parametric phantom-msg ADT: `type Element msg = Empty | Text String | Container (List Attr) (List (Element msg))`

`msg` is phantom at use (Sky.Ui's Element). Emit a **non-generic** sealed interface plus variants whose payloads don't reference `msg` (because msg doesn't appear in field types here — only in event-attribute payloads which carry their own typed slot). Where msg DOES flow (Container's nested Element list), the typed list element type is the interface itself (`Std_Ui_Element`), so recursion works without Go generics.

```go
type Std_Ui_Element interface {
    _sky_adt_Std_Ui_Element()
    SkyName() string
}

type Std_Ui_Element_Empty_V     struct{}
type Std_Ui_Element_Text_V      struct{ V0 string }
type Std_Ui_Element_Container_V struct {
    V0 []Std_Ui_Attribute       // attribute list
    V1 []Std_Ui_Element          // nested children — recursive on the interface
}

func (Std_Ui_Element_Empty_V)     _sky_adt_Std_Ui_Element() {}
func (Std_Ui_Element_Text_V)      _sky_adt_Std_Ui_Element() {}
func (Std_Ui_Element_Container_V) _sky_adt_Std_Ui_Element() {}
// + SkyName() impls + gob.Register + RegisterAdtVariant.

var Std_Ui_Element_Empty Std_Ui_Element = Std_Ui_Element_Empty_V{}
func Std_Ui_Element_Text(v0 string) Std_Ui_Element { return Std_Ui_Element_Text_V{V0: v0} }
func Std_Ui_Element_Container(v0 []Std_Ui_Attribute, v1 []Std_Ui_Element) Std_Ui_Element {
    return Std_Ui_Element_Container_V{V0: v0, V1: v1}
}
```

Where msg ACTUALLY flows (event-attribute payloads — `onClick : msg -> Attribute msg`), Attribute itself goes the Go-generic route (case c shape) so the msg type round-trips.

### (c) Parametric real-flow ADT: `type Maybe a = Just a | Nothing`

When the type parameter appears in a constructor field, emit a Go-generic sealed interface + generic variant struct.

```go
type Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe[T any] interface {
    _sky_adt_Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe(T)        // marker takes T to bind the type param
    SkyName() string
}

type Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Just_V[T any]    struct{ V0 T }
type Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Nothing_V[T any] struct{}

func (Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Just_V[T])    _sky_adt_Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe(T) {}
func (Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Nothing_V[T]) _sky_adt_Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe(T) {}
func (Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Just_V[T])    SkyName() string { return "Just" }
func (Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Nothing_V[T]) SkyName() string { return "Nothing" }

func Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Just[T any](v0 T) Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe[T] {
    return Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Just_V[T]{V0: v0}
}
func Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Nothing[T any]() Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe[T] {
    return Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe_Nothing_V[T]{}
}
```

Coexistence with current `rt.SkyMaybe[T]`: during Phase 2 the codegen aliases `type Sky_Core_Maybe_Maybe[T any] = rt.SkyMaybe[T]` at the interface level so existing `rt.MaybeCoerce[int]` consumers still link. Phase 2 then ports `rt.SkyMaybe` to the new sealed-interface shape (the struct layout stays — gob compatibility — only the entry-point becomes an interface).

runtimePlan.emissionStrategy:
CODEGEN-SIDE NEW SHAPE:
  // Sealed iface (parameterised on type-vars when ADT is polymorphic).
  type Std_Ui_Element[Msg any] interface{ isStd_Ui_Element_(Msg) }

  // Per-variant concrete struct. Tag REMAINS as an unexported const for
  // tag-int comparisons (preserves auto-TCO / case-of lowering perf).
  type Std_Ui_Element_Node_V[Msg any] struct {
      NodeName string
      Attrs    []Std_Ui_Attr[Msg]
      Children []Std_Ui_Element[Msg]
  }
  func (Std_Ui_Element_Node_V[Msg]) isStd_Ui_Element_(Msg) {}

  // Constructor: variant-typed return, NOT SkyADT.
  func Std_Ui_Element_Node[Msg any](n string, a []Std_Ui_Attr[Msg], c []Std_Ui_Element[Msg]) Std_Ui_Element[Msg] {
      return Std_Ui_Element_Node_V[Msg]{n, a, c}
  }

RT-SIDE REFERENCE STRATEGY:
  1. rt.SkyADT REMAINS in rt.go as the legacy alias type — kept indefinitely as a backward-compat shape for: (a) external user-supplied Go FFI kernels that still type-assert to rt.SkyADT, (b) Sky.Core.Error builders (`makeError`, `errorKindAdt`) until they migrate, (c) `__sky_send`-injected events via `adtTagRegistry`.
  2. Introduce rt.SkyVariant marker interface: `type SkyVariant interface{ skyVariantTag() int; skyVariantName() string }`. Each emitted variant struct implements this via codegen-emitted methods (`func (Std_Ui_Element_Node_V[M]) skyVariantTag() int { return 0 }` etc.).
  3. rt-side dispatch helpers (AdtTag, AdtField, isSkyADT, deepEq, Coerce, EnumTagIs) get a unified "any → (tag, fields-by-index OR fields-by-name)" prologue that type-switches in priority order: `case SkyADT` (legacy), `case SkyVariant` (new), `default reflect fallback`.
  4. Pattern-match emission in Compile.hs switches from `rt.AdtTag(subj)` + `rt.AdtField(subj, i)` to Go type switches: `switch v := subj.(type) { case Std_Ui_Element_Node_V[Msg]: ... use v.NodeName, v.Children ... }`. The Tag-int compare path stays for the Can.Enum (all-nullary) optimisation since type-switches on N variants compile to identical jump tables.
  5. Generic monomorphisation: codegen MUST emit type args at every constructor call + every case-of subject ascription site. The PR-17b LowerCtx already knows these (Issue #521 path). Sealed iface variant structs are parameterised on the same TVars the alias was — no new inference work.

runtimePlan.patternMatchStrategy:
CURRENT (SkyADT tag-int dispatch):
  switch rt.AdtTag(msg) {
  case 0: // Increment
      _ = rt.AdtField(msg, 0).(int)
      ...
  case 1: // Decrement
      ...
  }

NEW (typed Go type switch):
  switch v := msg.(type) {
  case Msg_Increment_V:
      // v has no fields (nullary)
      newCount := count + 1
  case Msg_AddN_V:
      // v.N is typed `int`, NOT any.
      newCount := count + v.N
  case Msg_SetLabel_V:
      // v.Label is typed `string`.
      newLabel := v.Label
  default:
      panic(rt.Unreachable("Msg pattern non-exhaustive"))
  }

CONCRETE WALKER — Html.map equivalent (the canonical recursive ADT walker):
  // OLD shape (SkyADT-driven, with reflective field access):
  func Std_Html_map(fn any, html any) any {
      a := html.(SkyADT)
      switch a.Tag {
      case 0: // Element
          name := a.Fields[0].(string)
          attrs := AsList(a.Fields[1])
          children := AsList(a.Fields[2])
          mappedAttrs := List_map(attrFn(fn), attrs)
          mappedChildren := List_map(SkyCall_partial(Std_Html_map, fn), children)
          return SkyADT{Tag: 0, SkyName: "Element", Fields: []any{name, mappedAttrs, mappedChildren}}
      case 1: // Text
          return a // text doesn't carry msg
      ...
      }
  }

  // NEW shape (sealed iface, typed payloads, NO reflection):
  func Std_Html_map[A, B any](fn func(A) B, h Std_Html_Html[A]) Std_Html_Html[B] {
      switch v := h.(type) {
      case Std_Html_Element_V[A]:
          mappedAttrs := make([]Std_Html_Attribute[B], len(v.Attrs))
          for i, a := range v.Attrs { mappedAttrs[i] = Std_Html_Attribute_map(fn, a) }
          mappedChildren := make([]Std_Html_Html[B], len(v.Children))
          for i, c := range v.Children { mappedChildren[i] = Std_Html_map(fn, c) }
          return Std_Html_Element_V[B]{Name: v.Name, Attrs: mappedAttrs, Children: mappedChildren}
      case Std_Html_Text_V[A]:
          return Std_Html_Text_V[B]{Content: v.Content}
      case Std_Html_Lazy_V[A]:
          return Std_Html_Lazy_V[B]{Thunk: func() Std_Html_Html[B] { return Std_Html_map(fn, v.Thunk()) }}
      default:
          panic(Unreachable("Std_Html_map: unknown variant"))
      }
  }

EXHAUSTIVENESS: Go vets `switch v := x.(type)` against the closed interface set (since the marker method is unexported, no out-of-package implementor is possible). Sky's existing exhaustiveness checker continues to fire at canonicalisation; the Go-side type switch is now a SECOND gate — defence in depth.

PERF: type-switches on N variants compile to a single jump table (same as int Tag compare). Net wins: zero reflect on payload access, zero `.(T)` assertion on Fields[i], zero Coerce calls on payload extraction.
